WEBVTT

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.780
<i>This dream again...</i>

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.020
If there's something you want 
to tell me, just say so!

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.280
<i>Or... Is this something that 
will happen in the future?</i>

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.610
Is it a premonition?

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.100
<i>I know...</i>

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:57.610
<i>who that is.</i>

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:08.120
<b>Sakura and the Crazy Sweets</b>

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.500
What's goin' on?

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.840
That was a heck of a fall!

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.500
I know... who that is.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.160
Sakura!

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.790
Wh-What's wrong, Sakura? Keep it together.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.280
Do ya recognize me? I'm Kero-chan.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.040
Did ya hit somethin' when ya 
fell? Does your head hurt?

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.360
Do ya have a bump? How many?

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.780
Pain, pain, go away! 
Go on, go away! Oh, man!

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.410
<i>I don't know... Who was it?</i>

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.280
Hey, Sakura!

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.780
<b>Hey, Sakura!</b>

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.210
Oh! Sorry, Kero-chan!

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.590
What'd ya do that for?

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.230
I'm sorry! Are you okay?

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:03.430
Y-Yeah. What about you? Are you okay?

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.250
You fell out of bed and got all spaced-out...

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:07.190
Yeah.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.680
I have to hurry!

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.730
But it's way earlier than usual.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.400
I promised to meet someone.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.470
Who?

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:26.240
<b>Tomoeda Central Park</b>

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.740
Rika-chan!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.700
Morning, Sakura-chan.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:41.840
<b>Tomoeda Central Park</b>

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.240
What?

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.840
I was just thinking that you 
look even more grown-up.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.380
And you look even more beautiful.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.090
Here's the picture book you asked for.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.340
Are you sure I can have it?

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.310
I've had plenty of time to read it.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.230
And that transfer student...

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.690
Akiho-chan!

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:05.190
If it'll make Akiho-chan happy, it's yours.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:06.780
Thanks!

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:12.960
I also added some that I think 
are ideal for reading aloud.

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:14.830
Use them, too, if you like.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.710
Thanks!

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:27.970
<b>Tomoeda Central Park</b>

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:20.250
You're going to be reading to 
children at the hospital, right?

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.370
That's amazing.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.490
It's really not amazing at all.

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:27.030
I'm just doing it to help 
my brother's friend.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:32.550
You'll have to get going, so you 
can get to school in time, huh?

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:33.530
Yeah...

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:36.030
Sorry. I know you got up early for this.

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:39.480
No problem! I'm glad I got to see you!

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.020
Me, too.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.970
Let me know when you all 
get together again, okay?

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:46.450
I'd like to meet Akiho-chan, too.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.430
Sure!

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.480
Well, I'd better go.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.860
I wish we could talk longer...

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.790
Sorry I made you go out of your way.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.410
Don't worry about it. See you later.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.360
See you.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.080
That was nice.

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.400
Yeah! I can't wait to read the picture book!

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.950
And I got to talk to Rika-chan, too.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.590
And now that you're all happy, 
I have news for ya.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.720
You're cooking in Home Ec Class today, right?

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:19.540
Yeah.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.600
Your apron ain't in here.

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:37.280
M-Morning!

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:43.160
Morning. I saw you running, flat-out.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:46.790
I... I had to go back for my apron.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:48.590
Are you all right?

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:49.870
Y-Yeah.

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:52.890
That was a magnificent run!

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:58.280
I hear we're making desserts 
in Home Ec, today.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:06:59.640
I can't wait.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:00.870
Me, either.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.900
You can even make extras to give someone.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.800
Someone special to you.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:13.210
I love roll cakes!

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:14.360
Me, too!

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.430
Well, then, let's do our best.

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.580
Yeah!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.540
<b>Parchment Paper</b>

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.720
Are you doing okay, Akiho-chan? 
Need to switch?

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.540
I'm still all right.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.340
It's starting to turn whiter.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:41.480
When it turns viscous, it's ready.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:43.090
Viscous?

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.200
It's like... "nnnngh!"

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.610
"Nnnngh"?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.470
Like, "nnnngh!"

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.720
Like, "nnnngh!"

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:56.240
These egg whites have turned into meringue.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.240
Way to go, Tomoyo-chan!

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:04.260
Now, we just sift baking powder and 
cake flour into the egg yolk batter.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:06.990
Then mix it some more.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.050
Are you doing all right, Sakura-san?

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.480
Do you need to switch?

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:15.090
Not yet. I'm okay for now.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:20.510
Put half of the meringue in the batter.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.510
Slowly...

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:25.540
Then add the rest of the meringue.

00:08:25.850 --> 00:08:27.850
Slowly, carefully...

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:31.310
Pour the batter into the pan.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:34.330
And then bake it in the oven!

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.400
It turned out perfect!

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:40.820
We did it!

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:44.060
We can decorate it however we want, right?

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:48.500
Yes, since they're single-serving mini rolls.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.590
There, all done!

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:56.840
You're giving yours to Kaito-san, right?

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:00.120
How are you going to decorate it?

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.530
I... I was thinking of making it a clock.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:03.660
A clock?

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:04.480
Yes.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:10.500
Like the pocket watch Kaito-san always wears.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.740
It seems to be very important to him.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:15.200
What about you?

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:15.780
Huh?

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.250
I-I'm not sure.

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:22.150
A compass... would probably be too hard,

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:24.560
so maybe something cute...

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.360
Compass?

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:32.590
What about the thing you have on 
your smartphone, Kero-san?

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:34.000
K-Kero-chan?

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:40.070
That might make it kind of hard to eat.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.390
True... I can see why you 
would feel bad, eating it.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:52.350
By the way, Akiho-chan, you didn't have 
that bunny on your bag, today.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:57.870
I caught Momo's scarf on something...

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:02.580
Kaito-san is home, mending it.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.760
There. All finished.

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:26.890
Honestly...

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:31.480
That girl will never grow out of her clumsiness.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.950
That's part of what makes her so cute.

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.480
Yes, I suppose so.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.330
Staying still all the time is exhausting...

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:43.830
Your effort is appreciated.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:46.720
Here. Have some chocolates.

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:53.170
The most delicious and
beautiful food in the world!

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:03.640
So?

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:08.290
Has the time still not arrived?

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:12.450
The collection of cards is proceeding steadily.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:15.520
We are indeed progressing...

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.850
toward that time.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:22.650
Yes...

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:29.630
Even now.

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:40.130
Hey, know what? I met up with 
a friend of mine, today.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:42.390
One from elementary school.

00:11:43.210 --> 00:11:44.550
Rika-chan!

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:46.550
Oh! Was she doing well?

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:49.330
Yeah. We met up this morning,

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.670
and she gave me a book.

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:52.680
A book?

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:54.330
It looked really interesting!

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:57.200
It's the kind with pictures that 
pop out of the pages,

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.330
and it's about Alice.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:11:59.440
Alice!

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:04.050
I wanted to show you, 
so I meant to bring it...

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:08.990
But when I went back for 
my apron, I left it there.

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:10.250
Oh, dear.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:13.190
I'm sorry. I'll definitely bring it tomorrow.

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:16.920
Don't worry about it!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.450
I'll look forward to tomorrow!

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.210
Akiho-chan...

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:22.960
Thanks!

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:26.580
Thank you for the book, too.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:29.270
What the?!

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:45.480
What's going on?!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.220
Sakura-chan...

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:53.620
Yeah. We have to do something about everyone.

00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:59.530
Sakura-chan, how about here?

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.070
<i>Release...</i>

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:16.770
Make everyone sleep!

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:18.520
<i>Snooze!</i>

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:42.620
Is it another card?

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:44.710
I think so.

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:52.950
They're very cute, yes?

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:54.010
Yeah.

00:13:54.780 --> 00:13:57.510
They don't seem to be causing any harm...

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:21.920
Sakura!

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:22.790
Kero-chan!

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.770
No one saw you, right?

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:26.910
We're good... Everyone's asleep.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:29.340
More importantly, what happened?

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.520
What the heck is that?!

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:34.320
It's a roll cake.

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:36.200
That thing ain't edible!

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:44.330
On what planet do roll cakes 
grow fangs and chase people?!

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:56.280
You hide here, Tomoyo-chan.

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:57.040
Okay!

00:14:58.260 --> 00:14:59.070
Kero-chan!

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:01.150
Take this.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.550
Leave it to me!

00:15:09.730 --> 00:15:12.120
Did it get even bigger?

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:14.630
Sakura, go from above.

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:15.490
Right.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:17.470
<i>Flight!</i>

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:27.410
All right, now it can't attack us.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.040
It can fly, too?!

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:35.790
This is good.

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:37.950
How do ya figure?

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:41.330
If we're in the sky, no one can get hurt!

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:56.340
Close it in!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.150
<i>Spiral!</i>

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:24.200
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:29.220
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.730
<i>Secure!</i>

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:46.810
"Appear."

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:51.350
Nice goin', Sakura!

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:49.980
<b>Appear</b>

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.530
What's wrong?

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:59.030
<b>Appear</b>

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:55.980
I just learned these characters.

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:58.580
"Ken... gen."

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:02.000
It means "to appear clearly."

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:03.650
Sakura!

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.800
Syaoran-kun!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:16.220
Are you okay? Were you hurt?

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.670
I'm okay.

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:25.600
Sorry I couldn't help you.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:27.120
You don't have to...

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:36.160
Don't mind us.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:43.960
The next thing I knew, the roll cakes 
we'd decorated were gone.

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:46.030
All of them?

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:48.820
Yes, all of our roll cakes disappeared!

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.380
That is quite a mystery.

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:52.800
Yes, it was.

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.770
We remade them afterward,

00:17:55.770 --> 00:17:59.960
but we didn't have enough 
ingredients or time left, so...

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:00.640
Um...

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.480
Is it difficult for you to say?

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.030
No, not exactly...

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:11.540
Um...

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:13.270
H-Here!

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:14.230
Yes?

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:18.050
We were allowed to bring 
our roll cakes home...

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:22.400
So, um, it's for you.

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:28.860
Thank you very much.

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:33.420
Would you mind if I opened it?

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:35.550
What? Right now?

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.440
Is that a problem?

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:40.760
No, it's not, but... well...

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:43.340
I'm a bit nervous.

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:44.810
I can't wait.

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.380
It's very cute!

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:54.390
Really?

00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:56.380
It's a clock.

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:59.450
Could it be... this?

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:02.950
I... I meant for it to have 
a closer resemblance.

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:04.990
But...

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:07.260
It looks truly beautiful.

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:11.170
You didn't make it in your 
beloved Momo-san's image?

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:16.670
I thought about it, at first, but I 
would have felt bad eating it.

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:18.050
That makes sense.

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:25.640
Momo!

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:29.100
I mended her scarf.

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:35.270
Thank you!

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:41.080
Since we have this, let's eat it together.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:42.650
But it's before dinner.

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:45.700
It is important to eat proper meals,

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.660
but isn't it also important 
to eat delicious things

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:50.920
exactly when you want to eat them?

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:52.910
Yes!

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:04.920
It's delicious!

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:09.460
I made it with Sakura-san and Tomoyo-san.

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:11.620
We all worked in teams of three.

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:15.290
They both taught me what to do, 
so that I could easily understand.

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.360
That's wonderful.

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:20.970
Chiharu-san is the best at making sweets,

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:24.600
but Sakura-san and Tomoyo-san 
are very skilled, as well.

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:27.830
Come to think of it, 
after the cakes disappeared,

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.820
Sakura-san seemed very apologetic,
 for some reason.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.690
Forgive me.

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:40.660
N-No, u-um... I was just surprised.

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:41.870
Surprised?

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:44.210
You seemed to be enjoying yourself very much!

00:20:44.210 --> 00:20:46.640
U-Um, please...

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.590
Please laugh again.

00:20:57.170 --> 00:21:01.300
D-Did I say something strange again?

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:04.730
I'm studying as hard as I can,

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:08.620
but I still say things that are illogical 
or irrelevant, all the time...

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:14.370
I'm sorry.

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:21.380
There is nothing you need apologize for.

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:29.030
Merely having you do this for 
me makes me truly happy.

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:33.100
Kaito-san...

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:50.760
Even with your "D" magic,

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:53.820
you can't stop that book's time.

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:58.830
That is exactly why the 
new cards are necessary.

00:24:10.020 --> 00:24:12.360
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:20.270
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:20.270
<b>K</b>

00:24:13.020 --> 00:24:15.600
Don't watch it, feel it. 
"Leave it to Kero-chan!"

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:20.470
Today, it's finally here. I'm introducin' 
both of Sakura's opening costumes!

00:24:20.470 --> 00:24:23.560
Here's the first. The crown on her head, 
the decorations on her waist and nails,

00:24:23.560 --> 00:24:25.480
and her heels are made of crystal.

00:24:25.480 --> 00:24:27.610
Here's the current one. The vivid 
red gives it a powerful look.

00:24:27.610 --> 00:24:32.710
The gold accent has just the right effect, 
and the hearts everywhere are so cute!

00:24:32.490 --> 00:24:36.280
